Subject: [PATCH 184/190] staging: mmi-dptx: Fix modetest hang

commit fe598702b2de371f6139939df907a9065d6faf98 from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

While running modetest, the system hangs randomly on attempting to reset
MMI DC. The MMI DC needs to be reset when the pixel format changes.
When the DC is reset and a delay occurs in sending video data, the
MMI DPTx goes in a underflow state. This generates underflow interrupt
storm causing stall on the CPU and generating a stack dump like below -

